cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or pipeline, please cite it as below."
title: "District Evolution: canonical identity, lineage, and area crosswalks for Indian districts, 1951-2025"
version: 4.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Satyam
repository-code: "https://github.com/Satyamkumar2610/architecture"
abstract: >
  A reproducible pipeline that assigns stable canonical identities to Indian
  districts across nine boundary vintages (Stanford 1951-2021, Survey of India
  2025), derives administrative lineage from planar overlays of consecutive
  maps, links a compiled events register to those identities with a
  probabilistic (Fellegi-Sunter) model constrained by territorial footprint,
  and publishes exact area crosswalks from every census year to 2025
  boundaries. Every output is validated by executable data contracts and SQL
  invariants and is byte-reproducible.
keywords:
  - India
  - administrative boundaries
  - districts
  - historical GIS
  - crosswalk
  - record linkage
